# A COLOSSUS'S TREAD WITH NO FOOT IN IT (gen_treads.gd): what the island holds
# between one lap and the next. The straddling walker is staged four world hours
# before it next comes down here, so the craters stand empty: at the lip of one,
# looking in -- the forty-metre floor of bared rock with the ring the pad's rim
# pressed into it and the scars its six claws dragged out through the strata,
# plate and wreck crushed flat round its edge, the strata stepped up out of it
# and the spoil thrown over the old ground -- then down into the bowl, then from
# above, standing on its floor, and drawn out wide enough to hold the whole of it.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_crater.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0-240 --hour=12 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
near colossus_rim
wait 3
shot 00-at-the-lip-looking-in
mouse 0,160 0.5
wait 1
shot 01-down-into-the-bowl
near colossus_crater
hold shoulder
wait 1.5
shot 02-top-down-on-the-floor
zoom 110
wait 2
shot 03-top-down-the-whole-crater
release shoulder
